    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48255" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyatīra</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θυάτειρα,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of
			Lydia</i>, now <i>Ak-hissar</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
				44, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29, 31, § 115</span></i>;
			also, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyatīra</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i><span class="en">Liv. 37, 8,
				7</span></i>. — Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thyatīrēni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Thyatira</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30,
				33, § 126</span></i>.</div>
